WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:05.030
What how I met your mother means to me is that grief is temporary.
我如何认识你母亲对我来说意味着悲伤是暂时的。

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:12.183
Whether I've had a fantastic day or a terrible day, watching that show is always the right move for the mid.
无论我度过了美好的一天还是糟糕的一天，观看该节目始终是中途的正确选择。

00:00:12.183 --> 00:00:14.434
And there was this wonderful show.
于是就有了这场精彩的表演。

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:20.527
That was all about how the randomness of life is what gets you exactly where you need to be.
这就是关于生活的随机性如何让你准确地到达你需要的地方。

00:00:20.527 --> 00:00:24.765
Welcome to How We Made Your Mother, which I think we're calling.
欢迎收看《我们如何创造了你的母亲》，我想我们就是这样称呼的。

00:00:24.765 --> 00:00:29.600
This is our new podcast rewatching 208 episodes of How I Met Your Mother.
这是我们的新播客，重播 208 集《老爸老妈的浪漫史》。

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.659
I'm Josh Radner.
我是乔什·拉德纳。

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.979
and I played Ted Mosby on the show for nine seasons.
我在剧中扮演泰德·莫斯比九季。

00:00:33.979 --> 00:00:39.380
And I am thrilled to be joined by Craig Thomas who co-created the show along with Carter Bayes.
我很高兴克雷格·托马斯 (Craig Thomas) 加入，他与卡特·贝叶斯 (Carter Bayes) 共同创作了该剧。

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.179
Josh, somehow it has been 20 years since our show premiered.
乔希，不知怎的，我们的节目首播已经过去 20 年了。

00:00:42.179 --> 00:00:43.460
That can't be right, your math is off.
这不可能是对的，你的数学不行。

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.380
It seems wrong, I'm sure it's wrong, let's check it.
好像不对，肯定不对，我们检查一下。

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:51.420
But it's also been 10 years since the show went off the air and while deeply disturbing, it makes it a good time to look back.
但该剧已经停播十年了，虽然令人深感不安，但现在正是回顾的好时机。

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:57.780
Well, if you're a super fan, we're going to get into all the secrets, theories, easter eggs, slash pineapples, and general knowledge.
好吧，如果您是超级粉丝，我们将深入探讨所有秘密、理论、复活节彩蛋、切菠萝和常识。

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.780
General knowledge?
常识？

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:06.319
but we'll also use him-yim and our relationship to it, these 20 years later, to talk about life and love and art and everything in between.
但二十年后，我们也会用他和我们之间的关系来谈论生活、爱情、艺术以及介于两者之间的一切。

00:01:06.319 --> 00:01:10.640
And just like the show itself, this podcast doesn't exist without you.
就像节目本身一样，没有您就没有这个播客。

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.659
Your voices will be a big part of what we do.
您的声音将成为我们工作的重要组成部分。

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:21.340
I'm a loo, I will be soon in New York City.
我是个厕所，我很快就会到达纽约市。

00:01:22.459 --> 00:01:23.540
Tell the people listening.
告诉正在听的人。

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:28.099
How many times over has your wife, Tornana, seen how I met your mother?
你的妻子托尔纳娜看过多少次我是如何遇见你母亲的？

00:01:28.099 --> 00:01:29.700
It is zero times.
是零次。

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:40.540
But we have a section called, Questions and observations from a clinical psychologist, relationship expert, who's never seen how I met your mother who also happens to be married to Josh.
但是我们有一个部分叫做“临床心理学家、关系专家的问题和观察”，他从未见过我是如何认识你母亲的，而她恰好也嫁给了乔什。

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.939
Is that title too catchy?
这标题是不是太吸引人了？

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:46.340
We are now embarking on this rewatch together, our her first watch rather.
我们现在正在一起重新观看，这是我们的第一部观看。

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:51.980
A couple of times, when I was looking at Robin in a certain way, she would go, I know that look.
有几次，当我以某种方式看着罗宾时，她会说，我知道那种表情。

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.780
Uh-huh.
嗯嗯。

00:01:53.780 --> 00:02:00.299
When I see you, please permit me to tell you everything.
当我见到你时，请允许我告诉你一切。

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:03.939
But there's one guy owned the bar.
但这家酒吧的老板是一个人。

00:02:03.939 --> 00:02:05.859
He had never been off the island of Mallorca.
他从未离开过马略卡岛。

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:12.060
He said, How I met your mother has taught me that what's happening now will be my memories one day.
他说，我是如何认识你母亲的，这告诉我，现在发生的事情有一天会成为我的回忆。

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.900
So make sure that you're making good memories for yourself in the present moment.
因此，请确保您此刻正在为自己留下美好的回忆。

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:23.550
And this old man, he must have made a fell in love with you.
而这个老男人，一定已经爱上你了。

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.419
And New York City.
还有纽约市。

00:02:26.419 --> 00:02:28.219
I'm excited to unpack this stuff.
我很高兴能拆开这些东西。

00:02:28.219 --> 00:02:32.699
And it feels honestly, It feels like psychologically healthy for me to do this, you know?
老实说，这样做对我来说心理上是健康的，你知道吗？

00:02:32.699 --> 00:02:35.060
It feels like are you ready to go back to the Titanic?
感觉就像你准备好回到泰坦尼克号了吗？

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:36.060
You know?
你知道？

